3. MANDATORY ATTRIBUTION AND ACADEMIC CITATION (CREDIT REQUIREMENT)
Whenever 'pyfossil' or 'FOSSIL' is utilized, directly or indirectly, to generate data, 
numerical results, tables, graphs, figures, or simulation models presented in any public 
or academic work, you MUST provide explicit credit to the Author as follows:

  a. Scientific Citation: You must cite the primary peer-reviewed publications describing 
     the underlying numerical formulations and mechanistic models:

     - de Paula, F. F., Igreja, I., Quinelato, T. O., & Chapiro, G. (2024). 
       Numerical simulation of foam displacement impacted by kinetic and equilibrium 
       surfactant adsorption. Advances in Water Resources, 188, 104690. 
       https://doi.org/10.1016/j.advwatres.2024.104690

     - de Paula, F. F., Igreja, I., & Chapiro, G. (2026). 
       Gas-dependent mobility control in foam-assisted injection: Comparative analysis 
       of CO2 and N2 in heterogeneous reservoirs. Gas Science and Engineering, 154, 205968. 
       https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jgsce.2026.205968

     - de Paula, F. F., Igreja, I., Quinelato, T. O., & Chapiro, G. (2023). 
       A numerical investigation into the influence of the surfactant injection technique 
       on the foam flow in heterogeneous porous media. Advances in Water Resources, 171, 104358. 
       https://doi.org/10.1016/j.advwatres.2022.104358

  b. Acknowledgment Statement: In all published papers, preprints, conference proceedings, 
     theses, or presentations, an acknowledgment statement must be included:
     "Numerical simulations were conducted using pyfossil (FOam diSplacement SImuLator), 
